AI Stock Pool includes generated research snapshots that reference third-party
market data, company names, news feeds, public web pages, and arXiv metadata.

The MIT License applies to the source code in this repository. It does not
grant rights to third-party data or content. Users are responsible for
complying with the terms, attribution requirements, and redistribution rules
of each original provider.

The project is provided for research and educational use. It is not investment
advice, a solicitation, or an automated trading service. Data can be delayed,
incomplete, or incorrect.

Adaptation: mobile-briefing.ts is a TypeScript adaptation of ai-stock-pool's
mobile_briefing.py (Copyright (c) 2026 Yaolei, MIT), supplied via
.local/product-definition/reuse-sources/ai-stock-pool/mobile_briefing.py.
Reused: ticker reference parsing, company-name lookup, reference filtering,
source object and selected list mapping. Adapted to ContentBundle/A-share
codes; no generated data or preset stock pool copied. Unknown publication
stays unknown (no creation/observation fallback); freshness uses actual
publication age and rejects future timestamps, not mere row presence.
